<title>SINGAPORE: Malayan Credit 1st-half net rises 88 pct.</title>
<headline>Malayan Credit 1st-half net rises 88 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  31.18   vs   16.61</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)		8.50   vs    4.70</p>
<p>    Turnover			    83.50   vs   55.42</p>
<p>    Associates (group share)	26.46   vs    nil</p>
<p>    Operating profit		  30.33   vs   20.08</p>
<p>    Share of results of	     11.00   vs    nil</p>
<p>associates</p>
<p>    Net interest income		2.18   vs    3.09</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    43.52   vs   23.17</p>
<p>    Tax				   12.16   vs    6.63</p>
<p>    Minorities		 (loss)  0.18   vs    0.07 (gain)</p>
<p>Note - Malayan Credit Ltd, a unit of car retailer Cycle &amp; Carriage Ltd, is a property developer.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
